Already there:
{liste}

soutien.description:
Vision is free and open source. If you'd like to thank the project, you can buy me a coffee: {lien}

In return, a "Supporter" badge appears and the Vision eye occasionally winks, with a small heart, on the screensaver and in "About". It is purely decorative: no feature is locked.

The code you receive by e-mail is checked here, offline: nothing is sent anywhere.

code_gestion.description:
{etat}

This code releases, on a PC, a message that blocks “until released”. It can only be set here (administrators): the Vision window on the PC can no longer choose it. Home Assistant keeps only its fingerprint and checks it itself; the PC keeps nothing. After {essais} wrong codes on a PC, its tries are paused for {minutes} minutes; after {total} wrong codes in 24 h across the whole place, the code is locked until it is changed here.

6 to 32 characters. A code typed on a PC goes through the Requester's session: do not type it in front of them, and change it if in doubt. A blocking message can also be released from Home Assistant (“Release a message” action), without a code.

code_octroi.description:
{etat}

A Decider's unlock code is the same in the Vision app and in the dashboard: it is asked on EVERY action that grants something (accepting a request, unlocking, giving time, opening, allowing, approving a device, giving a role). Usually the Decider chooses it in the app; here you can set, change or remove it (forgotten code, locked code). Home Assistant only keeps its hash; the fingerprint stays available on their devices. After {essais} wrong codes, an account or device waits {minutes} minutes; after {total} wrong codes in 24 h, everything is locked until a code is set again.

At least 4 characters.
